# Wave T50 (Fenland kit): walkfloor — Fenland City's registered street kind (the fleet's street kinds carry the -floor suffix; the desire-path tiers key on it). MARSH BOARDWALK: horizontal weathered-olive planks laid as a raised walkway — seams every 4 px, staggered end joints with dark pegs, a pale worn centre band where feet pass, wet dark plank feet. The town form 'great-marsh boardwalk reed' (TOWN_STYLE) laid as a street: the boardwalk the town sign and the audit row name, become the street graph itself. A PLANK DECK: unlike Bridgeport's ringfloor (ring-inset quay flags), Heritage's heritagefloor (cross-hatched flagstone), Repose's pebblefloor (rounded pebbles), Shardfall's shardfloor (cracked slate), Honeyfield's honeyfloor (hex comb), Clover's cloverfloor (flecked earth) — and unlike the harbour boardwalks of Arcport/Driftlog (grey-brown ship timber, nailed): Fenland's is olive marsh timber, pegged, worn pale at the centre. (NO-SAME-KIT law; WAVE-T50-FENLAND-PLAN.md §5.)
